<!--
     Now Playing, userspace half. (The HAL half is a PAL stream_config for the
     model's vendor_uuid, carried in crdroid_onyx_patches as
     patches/vendor_xiaomi_onyx/0002-soundtrigger-google-music-detector.patch.)

     ASI gets its Now Playing configuration from the DeviceConfig namespace
     device_personalization_services, which GMS Phenotype populates at runtime.
     Google withholds a chunk of it from non-Pixel devices: the ASI prebuilt we
     ship references 106 NowPlaying__* flags and Phenotype delivers only 53 here.

     Almost all of the shortfall is harmless, but ONE of the missing flags is
     load-bearing: ambient_music_index_manifest_17_09_02 carries the URL of the
     song-database manifest, in the form "<version>:<manifest-url>". There is no
     compiled-in default anywhere in the APK - grep the dex and you will not find
     a single "music-iq" string. So with the flag absent, ASI has nothing to fetch
     and Now Playing sits on "Downloading song database" forever. That was the
     second of the two bugs that kept this feature dead on onyx.

     SimpleDeviceConfig re-applies these at every LOCKED_BOOT_COMPLETED with
     makeDefault=true, so they act as a FALLBACK: a later Phenotype sync can still
     override any of them. That layering is deliberate, and it is why this list is
     deliberately minimal - it sets only the three flags Phenotype demonstrably
     does not send to this device, and does not fight Google over the other 42 that
     it does send correctly. Overriding those would just pin them stale forever.

     In particular NowPlaying__dsp_model_checksum_enabled is NOT set here even
     though some Qualcomm Pixel trees (e.g. redbull) force it false. Phenotype
     sends it as true on onyx, and the model provably loads with it true -
     LOAD_MODEL -> 3 / START_RECOGNITION -> Binder, with no checksum complaint
     anywhere in the log. It was never part of the bug.

     THE DSP AUDIO SOURCE IS THE THIRD BUG, and ambient_music_use_dsp_audio_source
     below is the fix. PAL reports LOAD_MODEL/START_RECOGNITION success at the HAL
     boundary but the ADSP session underneath is inert: module_type CUSTOM1 resolves
     to CustomVAInterface, libcustomva_intf.so on this SoC is a Qualcomm stub, and
     ACDB carries no graph for it ("AcdbCmdGetGraphAlias Error[19]: Unable to find
     graph key vector", then graph_set_config -131 on every set_config). So ASI
     armed a session that could never deliver a buffer, and recognition_history
     stayed empty.

     ASI does not need that session. Recognition runs entirely in userspace here:
     libsense_nnfp_v3.so is the neural fingerprinter and music_detector.sound_model
     is a TFLite model ("TFL3" magic at offset 4), both inside the APK. The only
     thing the DSP was providing was the audio buffer, and there is a flag for that.
     Decompiled, the branch is unambiguous:

         iget-boolean v1, v1, Lyxc;->o:Z      # ambient_music_use_dsp_audio_source
         if-eqz v1, :cond_5e
         ...  "Creating AudioRecord accessing DSP audio."   -> Lyyx;->d(F)
       :cond_5e
         ...  "Creating AudioRecord accessing Mic audio (shouldn't happen)."
              new AudioRecord(0 /* DEFAULT/MIC */, 16000, CHANNEL_IN_MONO,
                              ENCODING_PCM_16BIT, size)

     The mic branch touches neither SoundTrigger nor Lyyx, so it needs no ACDB graph.
     Its "(shouldn't happen)" log string is Google's, and only means no Pixel ever
     takes it - the path is fully implemented, not a stub.

     NECESSARY BUT NOT SUFFICIENT - do not stop reading here. Tracing further up
     the ambient pipeline settles the question this flag does NOT answer:

       Lylv  = com/google/intelligence/sense/ambientmusic/buffer/AudioBufferManager
       Lyls  = its lambda, the branch above
       Lyyx  = the trigger object every stage consumes

     Lyyx has exactly one <init> call site in the whole APK, inside
       Lyyx;->b(Landroid/hardware/soundtrigger/SoundTrigger$RecognitionEvent;)
     which reflects "status" and "data" off the event. Its only two callers are
     Lyyp (extends android.media.soundtrigger.SoundTriggerDetectionService,
     onGenericRecognitionEvent) and Lyys (a BroadcastReceiver taking the event out
     of an Intent). SoundTrigger$RecognitionEvent is NEVER constructed inside the
     APK - grep for it and you get nothing.

     So the ambient pipeline is hard-gated on the framework delivering a real
     SoundTrigger recognition event. This flag changes where the audio comes from
     AFTER that event; it does not start anything. On onyx the session arms and
     stays inert, so no event ever arrives and the branch above is never reached.

     Keep the flag anyway: it is correct, it is free, and it is a prerequisite for
     any fix to the trigger - a synthesized event does not have to carry a usable
     DSP capture session if ASI is going to open its own mic AudioRecord.

     THE REMAINING BLOCKER, and it is tractable because we build frameworks/base:
     something has to hand ASI a SoundTrigger$RecognitionEvent. Lyys being a plain
     BroadcastReceiver is the opening. That is a real project, not a config change,
     and it belongs to a later phase.

     WHAT SHOULD ALREADY WORK ON onyx: on-demand recognition. Lyxx;->d() opens its
     own AudioRecord(1 /* MIC */, 16000, CHANNEL_IN_MONO, PCM_16BIT, 0x3e800) and
     drives android.media.musicrecognition.RecognitionRequest - the
     MusicRecognitionManager system API, no SoundTrigger anywhere. That is the
     "identify this song" button rather than passive ambient detection. Test that
     before assuming Now Playing is wholly broken.

     Two costs of taking the mic path, once the trigger exists: ASI holds a real
     mic AudioRecord instead of a low-power DSP island, so expect the mic privacy
     indicator and measurably worse standby drain.

     The flag itself is still worth setting live before trusting a build:

         adb shell device_config put device_personalization_services \
             NowPlaying__ambient_music_use_dsp_audio_source false

     then play music near the device and watch `adb logcat -s AmbientMusic`.

     One more thing to verify on device rather than assume. SimpleDeviceConfig
     calls DeviceConfig.setProperty(..., makeDefault=true) once per
     LOCKED_BOOT_COMPLETED. That survives a resetToDefaults, but it does NOT
     survive a Phenotype sync that explicitly pushes the same key - and this key
     may or may not be in the 53 flags Phenotype actually sends to a non-Pixel
     (the APK references 106). So after a boot, confirm the value stuck:

         adb shell device_config get device_personalization_services \
             NowPlaying__ambient_music_use_dsp_audio_source

     If it reads back true, Phenotype is overwriting us and the flag has to be
     pinned another way (e.g. blocking the ASI Phenotype sync, or setting it from
     a later-running hook than LOCKED_BOOT_COMPLETED).

     REFRESHING THE CORPUS: the version/URL below pins a specific database build,
     so it will slowly go stale and start missing very recent releases (recognition
     of everything already in it keeps working). To refresh, take the current value
     from a Pixel device tree that crDroid still maintains, e.g.
     device/google/zumapro/overlay/SimpleDeviceConfigOverlayZumapro/res/values/config.xml.
     Do not hand-edit the date in the URL - the numeric prefix is a corpus version
     that has to match the manifest, and a mismatch is rejected.
-->
<resources>
    <string-array name="configs_device" translatable="false">
        <!-- The song database. This is the flag that actually fixes Now Playing. -->
        <item>device_personalization_services/NowPlaying__ambient_music_index_manifest_17_09_02=3161:https://storage.googleapis.com/music-iq-db/updatable_db_v3/20260118-030028/manifest.json</item>
        <!-- Gates the on-demand "search for this song" button against the
             installed Google App version. Withheld here; without it the button
             stays hidden even when a new enough AGA is present. -->
        <item>device_personalization_services/NowPlaying__on_demand_min_supported_aga_version=12.35.17</item>
        <!-- Page size for the recognition-history list. Withheld here; defaults
             to something much smaller, which truncates the history view. -->
        <item>device_personalization_services/NowPlaying__recognition_history_page_size=1000</item>
        <!-- Take audio from the mic rather than the DSP island. Defaults to true
             in the APK (myz.<clinit>: const/4 v0,0x1 -> Boolean.valueOf -> the
             NowPlaying__ambient_music_use_dsp_audio_source qvp), and true is
             unsatisfiable on onyx - see the DSP note above. Necessary but not
             sufficient: the ambient pipeline is separately gated on a real
             SoundTrigger event that onyx never delivers. -->
        <item>device_personalization_services/NowPlaying__ambient_music_use_dsp_audio_source=false</item>
    </string-array>
</resources>
